From c0232effb7f130368a4053d5491fabdfc7cd6c73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yomathnotcool <125728853+DengZhiyuan-math@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:45:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: a Pursue's total turns and time limit are shown before
 Start and submitted with it (#18)

proof-agents#19 fixes one total of turns and one time limit for each
Pursue at its Start. The hub passes PursuitHooks its node budget, shows
default_limits() before Start (the project's Pursue and a subtree's), and
checks the researcher's {"turns", "minutes"} with proof-agents' own rule
before anything is recorded or started (INVALID_LIMITS, 400), then passes
them to Start. While it runs and after, the page shows the Pursue's turns
against the total, structure turns and failed launches apart, and the time
left; the subtree card also names the nodes the total interrupted (a
parent whose re-split it prevented) and those whose launches failed.

A Theorem's Coordinator asked for while the pursuit is not on it (its
default limits read the subtree) records no Theorem step. With a
proof-agents from before #19 the page shows no limits and Start sends none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
